FortiGate Vitual Appliance

Step 1: Login to Fortinet Support Account
Open a web browser
Go to https://support.fortinet.com
Login using your Fortinet account credential
If you do not have an account, create one and then log in.

Step 2: Open FortiGate VM Download Page
After successful login, directly open the following page:

FortiGate VM Download:

https://support.fortinet.com/Download/VMImages.aspx

Create a new VM with:

| Setting    |             Value                                    |
| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| CPU               | 1 Core                                        |
| RAM               | 2048 MB  |
| Disk              | 2 GB (System) + 30 GB (Data)                  |
| Network Adapter 1 | Bridged                                       |
| Network Adapter 2 | Bridged *(or Host-Only, if required)*         |

Boot the VM → On first login:
username: admin
password: (leave empty)

#Configure Network (Bridge Mode is Best)
#Inside VMware → set both adapters to Bridged.

#Set WAN Interface to DHCP
#In FortiGate CLI:

config system interface
    edit port1
        set mode dhcp
        set allowaccess ping https http ssh
    next
end

#Check IP:
get system interface physical

#Now open in browser:

https://10.0.0.90

#After booting the FortiGate virtual machine, log in for the first time using the following default credentials:

Username: admin
Password: (leave blank)
As soon as you press Enter, FortiGate will prompt you to create a new password.
Set a strong password and confirm it.

⚠️ Important:
Remember this username and newly created password, as these credentials will be required later to log in to the FortiGate GUI (web interface).

When accessing the FortiGate GUI, use the same admin username and password you created during the first login.

#Add Default Route + DNS
Default Route:
config router static
    edit 1
        set device port1
        set gateway 190.160.1.1
    next
end
DNS:
config system dns
    set primary 8.8.8.8
    set secondary 1.1.1.1
end

#Log in using the admin username and the password you created during the first login.

